## Subscription stack (storefront reality)

| Surface | App | Repo touchpoint |
|---------|-----|-----------------|
| **Replacement filter PDP** | **Appstle** | `templates/product.filter-replacement.json` — `appstle-subscription-product-page-widget` block; global embed `appstle-subscription-helper` in `config/settings_data.json` |
| Cart drawer upsells | Native Shopify `selling_plan_allocations` | `snippets/cart-drawer-upsell-*.liquid`, `assets/cart.js` — Appstle widget **does not** run in drawer (`settings_schema.json` note) |
| Headboard PDP | No Appstle block on default `product.json` | Filter subscription is separate product/template |

**Renewal shipping / billing** is configured in **Appstle admin** (shipping profiles, selling plans) and **Shopify Settings → Shipping and delivery** — not theme Liquid. Meeting notes: `content/meeting-notes.md`.

## Shopify CLI store connector (for live app/subscription queries)

Agents and developers should use **Shopify CLI store auth** so `shopify store execute` can read products, orders, and subscription contracts without guessing from Git alone.

**Store:** `airtulip.myshopify.com` (also in `shopify.theme.toml` → `[environments.development]`)

**One-time auth** (developer runs locally — opens browser):

```bash
shopify store auth --store airtulip.myshopify.com --scopes read_products,read_orders,read_shipping,read_customers,read_fulfillments,read_discounts,read_purchase_options,read_locations,read_price_rules,read_draft_orders
```

**Currently authenticated (2026-07-27):** `jesse@t2products.com` with the scopes above.

**Note:** `read_own_subscription_contracts` is a **protected** Subscription API scope (Partner app + Shopify approval). CLI store auth will fail with `missing_shopify_permission` if you include it. For subscription **contracts**, use the **Appstle merchant portal** or an approved custom app. CLI can still read **selling plans** via `read_products` + `read_purchase_options` on the filter product.

**Also protected (optional, request in Partner Dashboard if needed):** `read_all_orders` (orders older than 60 days — useful for long-running renewals).

**Invalid scopes to avoid:** `read_delivery_profiles` (use `read_shipping` instead).

**Verify:**

```bash
shopify store execute --store airtulip.myshopify.com --query "{ shop { name } }"
```

**Example — filter product selling plans:**

```bash
shopify store execute --store airtulip.myshopify.com --query "{ product(handle: \"replacement-filter-set\") { title sellingPlanGroups { name sellingPlans { id name } } } }"
```

Re-run `shopify store auth` with additional scopes if a query fails for missing scope. Theme dev/push remains developer-owned (`npm run dev` / staging publish) — CLI here is for **read/query** and app settings investigation.

## Redundancy / consolidation (worth confirming with the merchant)

- **Four subscription solutions** on one store: Shopify Subscriptions + Utterbond + PayWhirl + Appstle. Expect overlapping widgets, cart/checkout scripts, and support burden. Long-term, **one** subscription stack is usually ideal unless each serves a distinct business case.
- **Two email/SMS marketing platforms:** Klaviyo and Mailchimp. Often only **one** is needed; duplicates can mean duplicate popups, tracking, and list logic.
- **Affiliate / partnerships:** Collabs (Shopify) and UpPromote both present — confirm both are intentional.

## Theme repo touchpoints

- **PageFly:** Can add **alternate templates** and heavy **CSS/JS**; repo already includes `snippets/pagefly-main-js.liquid` and PageFly-related locale keys. When editing layout or performance, check whether PageFly pages bypass standard JSON templates.
- **Appstle (filters):** Product form sync — `assets/appstle-selling-plan-sync.js`, hidden `selling_plan` in `snippets/buy-buttons.liquid`. See `content/meeting-notes.md`.
- **Judge.me, Klaviyo, trust badges, etc.:** Often add storefront snippets or rely on app blocks — if something “mysterious” appears in the DOM, check app embeds before patching `theme.js` / `theme.css`.

## When working on this project

- Prefer **Shopify.dev** and each **app’s official docs** for integration limits (e.g. Online Store 2.0 vs checkout).
- After app install/uninstall, expect **orphaned** references in `config/settings_data.json` or templates — Theme Check and manual QA on staging.
